      const upd=()=>{if(ex)readout(ex,'<b>Smoke alarm</b>: americium-241 emits α particles that ionise the air between two plates, so a tiny current flows. Smoke absorbs the α particles, the current drops and the alarm sounds. α is safe here because it cannot get out of the case. <b>Thickness gauge</b>: β passes partly through paper; if the count rate falls the paper is too thick and the rollers adjust (α would be stopped completely, γ would pass straight through). <b>Tracer</b>: a γ emitter with a short half-life (technetium-99m, 6 h) is injected; a gamma camera outside the body shows where it collects (here, a kidney). <b>Sterilising and radiotherapy</b>: intense γ beams kill bacteria on sealed medical equipment, or cancer cells, aimed from several directions to spare healthy tissue.')};
