    conds:[{n:'menstrual cycle',r:'<b>Menstrual cycle</b> (infradian, ~28 days): rising oestrogen → ovulation mid-cycle; progesterone thickens the womb lining; if no pregnancy, hormone levels fall and menstruation begins · endogenous but affected by exogenous cues: <b>Stern and McClintock</b> — women exposed to others’ armpit pheromones had cycles that synchronised (68% changed) · small sample, other factors (stress, diet) matter'},{n:'seasonal affective disorder',r:'<b>SAD</b> (infradian, yearly): depression in winter months · less light → more melatonin secreted by the pineal gland → lower serotonin · treatment: phototherapy (light box for 2 hours a day) · Eastman: light therapy helped, but placebo effects were large'},{n:'90-minute sleep cycle',r:'<b>Ultradian sleep cycle</b> (~90 min): stage 1–2 light sleep (alpha → theta waves, sleep spindles), stages 3–4 deep slow-wave sleep (delta waves), then REM (fast, desynchronised waves, rapid eye movements, dreaming) · about 5 cycles a night; SWS more in early cycles, REM more later · <b>BRAC</b> (Kleitman): 90-minute alertness cycles during the day (Ericsson: violinists practised in 90-minute sessions)'}],
