    conds:[{n:'culture',v:[85,40,50],r:'<b>Culture</b>: religious food laws (halal, kosher, Hindu vegetarianism), cultural body ideals (Becker’s Fiji study), meal structures and portion norms (French vs American — Rozin: French ate smaller portions slowly) · food carries identity'},{n:'mood',v:[40,85,40],r:'<b>Mood</b>: stress and negative mood increase eating of energy-dense comfort foods in “emotional eaters” (Oliver: stressed women ate more sweet, fatty food) but reduce eating in others · Garg: people watching a sad film ate 36% more popcorn than those watching a comedy · boredom eating'},{n:'health concerns',v:[45,40,85],r:'<b>Health</b>: concerns about weight, heart disease and diabetes lead to dieting and choosing “healthy” labels · traffic-light labelling, sugar tax, 5-a-day campaigns · can backfire: restrained eaters may binge (restraint theory) · orthorexia — obsession with healthy eating'}],
