    conds:[{n:'method: gas syringe',r:'<b>Mg + 2HCl → MgCl₂ + H₂</b> · add 50 cm³ of 1.0 mol dm⁻³ HCl to the flask, add a 3 cm strip of Mg, <b>replace the bung immediately</b> and start the timer · read the syringe volume every 10 s until no more gas is made · repeat with 0.5, 1.5 and 2.0 mol dm⁻³ acid',d:D=>{D.fn('curve',x=>8*(1-Math.exp(-x*.5)),0x1C7ED6,'1.0 M',{from:0,to:10})}},{n:'method: mass loss',r:'<b>CaCO₃ + 2HCl → CaCl₂ + H₂O + CO₂</b> · flask of acid + marble chips on a balance, loose <b>cotton-wool plug</b> (lets CO₂ escape, keeps acid spray in) · record the mass every 30 s · mass lost = mass of CO₂ given off · plot mass loss against time',d:D=>{D.fn('curve',x=>7*(1-Math.exp(-x*.35)),0xE03131,'mass lost',{from:0,to:10})}},{n:'comparing concentrations',r:'<b>Results</b>: higher concentration → <b>steeper initial gradient</b> (more frequent collisions) but the same final volume if the metal is the limiting reactant · <b>mean rate</b> = total volume ÷ time taken (cm³/s) · <b>rate at time t</b> = gradient of the tangent · plot rate (or 1/time) against concentration to see the relationship',d:D=>{D.fn('curve',x=>8*(1-Math.exp(-x*1.0)),0xE03131,'2.0 M',{from:0,to:10});D.fn('curve',x=>8*(1-Math.exp(-x*.5)),0x1C7ED6,'1.0 M',{from:0,to:10,at:'end',ly:-.5});D.fn('curve',x=>8*(1-Math.exp(-x*.25)),0x2F9E44,'0.5 M',{from:0,to:10,ly:-.6})}},{n:'variables and errors',r:'<b>Independent</b>: acid concentration · <b>dependent</b>: volume of gas (or mass) over time · <b>control</b>: mass/length and surface area of solid, volume and temperature of acid · <b>errors</b>: gas escapes before the bung is in; syringe sticks; reading a moving scale; hydrogen is very light — mass loss is unsuitable for it · <b>safety</b>: eye protection, no flames near hydrogen',d:D=>{D.fn('curve',x=>8*(1-Math.exp(-x*.5)),0x1C7ED6,'',{from:0,to:10});D.fn('curve',x=>2.4+1.6*(x-1.5),0xE03131,'tangent',{from:.2,to:4.5});D.pt('curve',1.5,4.2,0xE03131)}}],
