    conds:[{n:'two particles over a pulley',v:[2.45,3.675],r:'<b>5 kg and 3 kg</b> hanging over a smooth pulley · A: 5g − T = 5a · B: T − 3g = 3a · add: 2g = 8a → <b>a = g/4 = 2.45 m/s²</b> · T = 3g + 3a = 3(9.8 + 2.45) = <b>36.75 N</b> · string tension is less than A’s weight, more than B’s'},{n:'particle on a table',v:[3.27,13.07],r:'<b>2 kg block on a smooth table</b> pulled by a 1 kg hanging mass: hanging: g − T = a · block: T = 2a → g = 3a → <b>a = 3.27 m/s²</b>, T = 6.53 N · with friction μ = 0.2 on the block: T − 0.2(2g) = 2a → a = 1.96 m/s²'},{n:'car and trailer',v:[.5,3.5],r:'<b>Car 1200 kg towing trailer 400 kg</b>, driving force 1500 N, resistances 500 N (car) and 200 N (trailer) · whole system: 1500 − 700 = 1600a → <b>a = 0.5 m/s²</b> · trailer: T − 200 = 400 × 0.5 → <b>T = 400 N</b> (bars show T ÷ 100) · when braking the tow-bar is in thrust'},{n:'after the string breaks',v:[9.8,0],r:'<b>If the string breaks</b> (or a particle hits the floor): tension becomes 0 · the falling particle accelerates at g · the other continues with its speed and decelerates (projected upward under gravity, or slows by friction on a table) · use suvat for the next stage · assumptions: light inextensible string, smooth light pulley, no air resistance'}],
