    conds:[{n:'uniform ladder alone',v:[196,56.6,56.6],r:'<b>Uniform ladder</b> 4 m, 20 kg (W = 196 N), at 60° to the ground against a smooth wall · vertical: R = 196 N · moments about the foot: S × 4 sin 60° = 196 × 2 cos 60° → <b>S = 56.6 N</b> · horizontal: F = S = 56.6 N · minimum μ = F/R = <b>0.289</b>'},{n:'with a person climbing',v:[882,229,229],r:'<b>Person 70 kg (686 N) 3 m up the ladder</b> · R = 196 + 686 = 882 N · moments about the foot: S × 3.46 = 196 × 1 + 686 × 1.5 → <b>S = 354 N</b>… (with a 60° angle: horizontal distances 1 m and 1.5 m) · F = S · if μ = 0.4, max F = 353 N → the ladder is just about to slip'},{n:'non-uniform rod',v:[150,0,0],r:'<b>Non-uniform rod</b> AB, 3 m, weight 150 N, supported at A and B with reactions 90 N and 60 N · moments about A: 60 × 3 = 150 × d → <b>d = 1.2 m</b> from A (centre of mass) · weight acts at the centre of mass, not the middle'},{n:'about to tilt',v:[0,0,0],r:'<b>Tilting</b>: a plank resting on two supports C and D with a load moving outwards · when it is about to tilt about D, the reaction at C becomes <b>zero</b> · take moments about D with R_C = 0 to find the critical position or mass · modelling: rod (rigid, no width), particle loads, smooth/rough contacts'}],
