    conds:[{n:'vectors and scalars',v:[12,4,0],r:'<b>Displacement</b> (vector): position from the origin, can be negative · <b>distance</b> (scalar): total path length · <b>velocity</b> (vector) vs <b>speed</b> (scalar) · a particle going 8 m right then 4 m left: displacement +4 m, distance 12 m',d:D=>{D.curve('g',[[0,0],[4,8],[8,4]],0x1C7ED6,'s–t',{r:.025})}},{n:'reading s–t graphs',v:[12,4,0],r:'<b>Displacement–time graph</b>: gradient = velocity · straight line = constant velocity · horizontal = at rest · curve = changing velocity (tangent for instantaneous velocity) · returning to s = 0 means back at the origin',d:D=>{D.curve('g',[[0,0],[3,6],[5,6],[9,0]],0x1C7ED6,'s',{r:.025})}},{n:'reading v–t graphs',v:[30,6,2],r:'<b>Velocity–time graph</b>: gradient = <b>acceleration</b>; area under the graph = <b>displacement</b> (areas below the axis are negative) · e.g. accelerates from 0 to 6 m/s in 3 s (a = 2 m/s²), steady for 4 s, decelerates to rest in 2 s → distance = 9 + 24 + 6 = 39 m',d:D=>{D.curve('g',[[0,0],[3,6],[7,6],[9,0]],0xE03131,'v',{r:.025});D.area('g',[[0,0],[3,6],[7,6],[9,0]],0xFFA8A8,.03,{glass:.6})}},{n:'constant vs variable acceleration',v:[39,6,2],r:'<b>Constant a</b>: suvat — v = u + at, s = ut + ½at², v² = u² + 2as, s = ½(u + v)t, s = vt − ½at² · <b>variable a</b> (given as a function of t): differentiate s to get v and a; integrate a to get v and s, using initial conditions for the constants'}],
