    conds:[{n:'three-figure bearings',v:[55,235,117],r:'<b>Bearing</b>: angle clockwise from <b>north</b>, three figures · N 000°, E 090°, S 180°, W 270°, NE 045° · A to B on a bearing of <b>055°</b> · always draw a north line at the point you measure FROM'},{n:'back bearings',v:[55,235,117],r:'<b>Back bearing</b>: bearing of A from B = 055° + 180° = <b>235°</b> · if the bearing is more than 180°, subtract 180° · alternate angles between parallel north lines explain why'},{n:'scale drawings',v:[55,235,117],r:'<b>Scale 1 : 50 000</b>: 1 cm on the map = 50 000 cm = 500 m · 6 cm → 3 km · real 7.5 km → 15 cm · draw: north line, measure the bearing with a protractor, mark the distance with a ruler · areas scale by the square of the ratio'},{n:'with trigonometry',v:[55,235,117],r:'<b>Calculating</b>: a ship sails 12 km on 055° then 8 km on 117° · the angle at B between the legs = 180° − 117° + 55° = 118° · cosine rule: AC² = 12² + 8² − 2(12)(8)cos 118° → AC = <b>17.2 km</b> · sine rule then gives the bearing of C from A'}],
