    conds:[{n:'know the context',v:[15.2,3.1,4],r:'<b>Context</b>: e.g. daily weather for several UK and international stations, May–October in two years · variables: max/min/mean temperature (°C), rainfall (mm), sunshine (h), windspeed (knots, Beaufort), gusts, humidity (%), cloud cover (oktas), visibility (dam), pressure (hPa) · coastal vs inland stations behave differently'},{n:'cleaning data',v:[15.2,3.1,4],r:'<b>Cleaning</b>: “n/a” or blank = missing — exclude and say so · <b>“tr”</b> = trace rainfall (< 0.05 mm) — treat as 0 · check for impossible values (e.g. humidity 120%) · outliers may be genuine (storms) · record every decision so results are reproducible'},{n:'calculations and charts',v:[15.2,3.1,4],r:'<b>Technology</b>: spreadsheets for means, standard deviations, PMCC, regression and histograms · compare stations or years with box plots · sample from the LDS using random or systematic methods · sense-check results against what you know about the climate'},{n:'exam-style judgements',v:[15.2,3.1,4],r:'<b>Familiarity questions</b>: “Would rainfall be normally distributed?” — no, it is skewed with many zero days · “Explain why the mean windspeed might be misleading” · “Is a linear model for temperature against sunshine reasonable for Hurn?” · use LDS knowledge to evaluate claims and suggest improvements'}],
