    conds:[{n:'application software',v:[80,40],r:'<b>Applications</b>: help users perform tasks · <b>general-purpose</b> (off-the-shelf word processor — cheap, well-tested, many features unused) · <b>special-purpose</b> (payroll, CAD) · <b>bespoke</b> (custom-written for one organisation — exactly fits needs, expensive, slow to develop)'},{n:'utility software',v:[80,40],r:'<b>Utilities</b>: <b>defragmentation</b> moves file fragments together on a magnetic disk (bars: access time ms) · <b>compression</b> (zip) · <b>backup</b> — full (everything) or incremental (only changes since last backup) · <b>encryption</b> · <b>anti-malware</b> · <b>disk cleanup</b> and file managers'},{n:'why defragment?',v:[80,40],r:'<b>Fragmentation</b>: as files are saved and deleted, new files are split into fragments across the disk · the read head must move more → slower · defragmenting puts fragments in order and groups free space · SSDs don’t need it (no moving parts, and extra writes shorten their life)'},{n:'open vs closed source',v:[80,40],r:'<b>Open source</b>: source code available; free to use, modify and share (often under GPL, MIT); community support; can audit security · <b>closed source</b>: compiled only; licence fee; vendor support, warranties and regular updates; protects intellectual property · also freeware (free, closed) and subscriptions'}],
