    conds:[{n:'utility software',v:[80,4,6,3],r:'<b>Utilities</b>: anti-malware (scan, quarantine, real-time protection), backup, compression, encryption, disk defragmentation, disk cleanup, file management, system monitoring (task manager) · they help maintain, protect and optimise the computer'},{n:'backups',v:[80,4,6,3],r:'<b>Full backup</b>: copy everything (bars: 80 GB) — simple restore, slow and large · <b>incremental</b>: only files changed since the last backup (4–6 GB) — fast and small, restore needs the full + every incremental · <b>differential</b>: changes since the last full · store off-site/cloud, test restores'},{n:'BIOS and drivers',v:[80,4,6,3],r:'<b>BIOS/UEFI</b>: firmware that tests hardware (POST) and loads the OS (bootstrap) · <b>device drivers</b>: translate OS commands into instructions for a specific device (printer, GPU) and handle its interrupts · both are system software'},{n:'virtual machines',v:[80,4,6,3],r:'<b>Virtual machines</b>: a hypervisor on the host shares CPU, RAM and storage among isolated guests (Linux, Windows, a test system) · snapshots allow instant rollback · used in cloud servers, testing, running legacy software, malware analysis · <b>process VMs</b> run bytecode (Java)'}],
