    conds:[{n:'arrays',v:[5,11,6],r:'<b>Array</b>: fixed number of items of the <b>same type</b>, contiguous in memory, accessed by index: marks[2] = 3 (zero-indexed) · 2D arrays for grids/tables: grid[row][col] · static (fixed size) vs dynamic (lists that grow)'},{n:'records',v:[5,11,6],r:'<b>Record</b>: a collection of related <b>fields</b> of different types describing one item · TYPE Student: name: STRING, age: INTEGER, enrolled: BOOLEAN · access with dot notation: s.name · an array of records models a database table'},{n:'tuples',v:[5,11,6],r:'<b>Tuple</b>: ordered, <b>immutable</b> collection, can mix types · point = (3, 4); colour = (255, 128, 0) · can’t change items after creation — safe for keys and fixed data · unpack: x, y = point · returned from functions to give several results'},{n:'vectors and user-defined types',v:[5,11,6],r:'<b>Vector</b> [3, 4]: magnitude √(3² + 4²) = <b>5</b>; with w = [1, 2]: dot product 3 + 8 = <b>11</b>; scalar 2v = [6, 8] · used in graphics, physics, machine learning · <b>user-defined types</b>: records, enumerations (ENUM Day = {MON, TUE…}), classes — model the problem clearly and let the compiler check types'}],
