    conds:[{n:'benefits and responsibilities',v:[9,5,5],r:'<b>Benefits</b>: global communication, e-commerce, online learning and healthcare, smart cities, automation, scientific research · <b>responsibility</b>: developers and companies decide what data to collect, what to build and how it can be misused · ask: who is affected, and how?'},{n:'privacy and surveillance',v:[7,9,5],r:'<b>Privacy</b>: personal data collected by apps, loyalty cards, smart devices, cookies — profiled and sold for targeted advertising · <b>surveillance</b>: CCTV with facial recognition, location tracking, workplace monitoring, government interception (RIPA 2000) · balance between security/crime prevention and individual liberty'},{n:'online harms and censorship',v:[7,7,5],r:'<b>Issues</b>: misinformation and deepfakes, cyberbullying, offensive content, radicalisation, addiction and mental health · <b>censorship</b>: governments filtering the internet; platforms moderating content — protects users but raises free-speech concerns · Online Safety Act duties on platforms'},{n:'digital divide and culture',v:[7,7,9],r:'<b>Digital divide</b>: unequal access to technology and skills — by income, age, location (rural broadband), disability, country · excluded from online services, jobs and education · cultural impacts: globalisation of media, changing social interaction, loss of local languages online · solutions: affordable access, digital skills training, accessibility design'}],
