    conds:[{n:'choosing the problem',v:[0,0,0,0],r:'<b>Choose wisely</b>: a real problem for a real client (club booking system, revision quiz app, simulation, game with AI) · enough complexity for high marks (OOP, complex algorithms, databases, recursion, networking) but achievable in the time · avoid copying tutorials'},{n:'identifying stakeholders',v:[3,0,0,0],r:'<b>Stakeholders</b>: the client (who commissioned it), end users (who use it daily), others affected (administrators, parents) · describe each group, their needs and how the solution helps them · keep a stakeholder in the loop for feedback throughout'},{n:'researching the problem',v:[3,25,2,3],r:'<b>Research</b>: interviews (open questions, record answers), questionnaires (larger sample, quantifiable), observation of current practice, analysis of documents · study <b>existing solutions</b> — features, strengths, weaknesses — and decide what to include or improve · bars: evidence gathered'},{n:'why it suits computation',v:[3,25,2,3],r:'<b>Computational methods</b>: explain how the problem can be <b>decomposed</b> into sub-problems, <b>abstracted</b> (ignore irrelevant detail), solved with <b>algorithms</b> and data structures, and benefits from automation/speed/accuracy · agree the <b>scope</b> and limitations with the client'}],
