    conds:[{n:'inputs and outputs',v:[5,150],r:'<b>Identify inputs and outputs first</b>: what data is needed, where it comes from (user, file, sensor, network), its type and format, and what must be output (screen, file, printer) · drives the choice of data structures and validation · e.g. a search: input search term, output matching items'},{n:'preconditions',v:[5,150],r:'<b>Preconditions</b>: requirements that must hold before code runs — binary search needs a <b>sorted</b> list; factorial needs n ≥ 0; a stack pop needs a non-empty stack · state them in documentation; the calling code checks them (or the subroutine validates) · makes subroutines simpler, reusable and easier to test'},{n:'caching',v:[5,150],r:'<b>Caching</b>: store recently/frequently used data or results for fast reuse — CPU cache, browser cache (images, pages), DNS cache, memoisation of function results · cache hit ≈ 5 ms vs fetching from the server 150 ms (bars) · <b>drawbacks</b>: uses memory, stale data if the original changes, complex to manage'},{n:'reusable components',v:[5,150],r:'<b>Reusable components</b>: libraries, modules, classes and APIs written once and used in many programs — saves development time, already tested and reliable, consistent · plan for reuse: general parameters, clear interfaces, documentation · e.g. a validation module used by every form'}],
