// ---------- Boy or girl, and family trees, in microscope and museum quality: the mother’s XX and father’s XY as real G-banded chromosomes, eggs with zona pellucida and corona radiata cells, swimming X- and Y-carrying sperm, and a glossy Punnett board whose boxes hold the XX or XY pair of each child; a family tree of polished acrylic symbols on brushed-metal lines (replaces the 'sex' and 'pedigree' views of LIB.genetics) ----------
