// ---------- Cloning and the fermenter, micromanipulation and industrial quality: an egg cell with its zona held by a glass holding pipette while a bevelled micropipette draws out its nucleus, an udder cell whose nucleus is carried across and injected, electrodes that spark to start division and an eight-cell embryo; a stainless fermenter cut away to show the broth of swirling microbes, Rushton turbine paddles on a motor-driven shaft, a sparger of rising air bubbles, the cooling-water jacket, temperature and pH probes and a valved product outlet (replaces the 'clone' and 'ferm' views of LIB.dnatech) ----------
